{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **6 November 2026**, Regulation 26(2)’s common-dealing-deadline requirement expressly permits:\n\n- **Cash versus in-kind:** different cut-offs for cash subscriptions/redemptions and in-kind subscriptions/redemptions.\n- **Class-level currency hedging:** different cut-offs for currency-hedged and unhedged classes where the currency hedging operates at class level.\n\nThese are **express regulatory exceptions**, not permissions requiring an individual waiver. The exceptions permit differing deadlines; they should not be paraphrased as invariably requiring cash or hedged-class deadlines to be earlier.\n\n**Older Q&A 1030:** this described a **case-by-case waiver application** for an earlier deadline for currency-hedged classes relative to unhedged classes. It was not a general exemption for arbitrary class-specific deadlines or the source of the express cash/in-kind exception.\n\n**Worth knowing:** distinguish what the amended regulation permits directly from what the older supervisory waiver process could accommodate."}}
